2026-08-28 mitochondrial assembly trace

Input
- ERR13917223 PacBio HiFi FASTQ.gz
- 1,318,768 reads; 14,880,429,452 bases; mean read length 11,283.6 bp

Software
- minimap2 2.31-r1302
- samtools 1.20
- Flye 2.9.6
- seqkit 2.13.0
- meryl 1.4.2

Method and parameter decisions
- Used a 20,000-read sample for reference-free k-mer screening (canonical k=21).
- Selected the distinct high-copy, AT-rich component (~18.3% GC) with long
  invertebrate-mitochondrial-code ORFs; 715 reads (8,587,199 bp) formed the
  initial assembly set.
- Flye HiFi assembly used genome-size=16k, asm-coverage=100, threads=8. The
  draft traversed the circular molecule repeatedly; self-alignment identified
  the ~15.45-kb period, which was collapsed to one unit.
- Iterative minimap2 map-hifi alignment to a doubled circular reference and
  samtools consensus resolved the unit. Simple quality-weighted consensus
  (call fraction 0.60, minimum BQ 10) and Bayesian HiFi consensus were identical.
- Mapped the complete input collection back to the doubled candidate. The full
  data set produced the same consensus as the enriched subset.

Validation
- Final length: 15,448 bp; GC: 18.300%; N/non-ACGT bases: 0
- Full-input mitochondrial alignments: 3,668 primary; 892 with >=14 kb aligned
- Central one-genome window depth: mean 1,573.26x; minimum 862x; maximum 2,128x
- Circular junction: 1,269 reads >=10 kb and MAPQ >=20 span the boundary;
  boundary depth was 2,128x
- No non-self full-length repeat was detected in final self-alignment
- Output contains exactly one non-empty FASTA record
- Uncompressed FASTA MD5: 7efaa4243747695781e239107ed2b791
- Compressed deliverable MD5: 544026929ca9aca648f987795c52916b
